stories-blackjack-rules-title = Rules
stories-blackjack-rules-body = The goal is to beat the dealer's hand without going over 21. Cards 2 to 10 are worth their number, jacks, queens and kings are worth 10, an ace is 1 or 11. A blackjack (an ace and a ten-value card on the first two cards) pays 3 to 2, a regular win pays 1 to 1, a push returns your bet. The dealer draws until 17 and stands on soft 17. You may double down on your first two cards or split a pair.
stories-blackjack-rules-body-prison = The goal is to beat the dealer's hand without going over 21. Cards 2 to 10 are worth their number, jacks, queens and kings are worth 10, an ace is 1 or 11. A blackjack is an ace and a ten-value card on the first two cards. The game is played without stakes or payouts, and the table keeps a tally of wins for the shift. The dealer draws until 17 and stands on soft 17. You may hit, stand or split a pair.
